<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Halicarnassus</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 377 BCE (approx.) · capital Halicarnassus</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Greek and Carian port city, birthplace of Herodotus and home of Queen Artemisia, which became the capital of Mausolus and the site of his Mausoleum.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Halicarnassus was founded by Dorian settlers from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/troezen">Troezen</a> on a bay of the Carian coast, beside native Carian communities, and the two populations mixed. It belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dorian-hexapolis">Dorian Hexapolis</a> but, according to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, was expelled after one of its citizens carried off a prize tripod.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> it was ruled by a Carian-Greek dynasty: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lygdamis-i">Lygdamis I</a> and his daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/artemisia-i-of-caria">Artemisia I</a>, who commanded ships for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-salamis">Salamis</a> in 480 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>, born there, opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lygdamis-ii">Lygdamis II</a> and went into exile. After the tyranny ended, Halicarnassus joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/delian-league">Delian League</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mausolus">Mausolus of Hecatomnid Caria</a> made Halicarnassus his capital in the 370s BCE, absorbing it into his dynastic state; his tomb, the Mausoleum, was a Wonder of the World. Alexander besieged the city in 334 BCE. It is modern Bodrum.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/halicarnassus.jpg" alt="Halicarnassus" width="320" height="212"><figcaption>Image: FollowingHadrian · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_ruins_of_the_Mausoleum_at_Halicarnassus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 377 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Halicarnassus</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Lygdamis I, Artemisia I, Lygdamis II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek and Carian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Doric Greek; Carian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Halikarnassos, Bodrum</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-638&amp;focus=halicarnassus" aria-label="Halicarnassus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5367 844 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Halicarnassus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5687 1100L5687 1100M5687 1100L6140 1251M5687 1100L5591 1068"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5687 1100h0M6140 1251h0M5591 1068h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5687 1100h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5687 1100h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-638&amp;focus=halicarnassus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
